<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mastarna</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">6th century BCE</span> · Also known as Macstrna</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mastarna (Etruscan Macstrna) was an Etruscan warrior shown in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francois-tomb">François Tomb</a> at Vulci freeing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caelius-vibenna">Caelius Vibenna</a>. The emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/claudius">Claudius</a>, in a speech preserved on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lyon">Lyon</a> Tablet, identified him with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/servius-tullius">Servius Tullius</a>, the sixth king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, citing Etruscan sources that made him Vibenna's companion who settled in Rome and changed his name.</p></div>
